# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TEST 6: Windows Defender Definitions Present
# Verify antimalware definitions file exists and is not empty
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
META
    esp_id `win-defender-definitions-present`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    control_framework `CIS`
    control `CIS-WIN-8.1`
    control_mapping `CIS:WIN-8.1`
    title `Windows Defender definitions must be present`
    description `Windows Defender requires up-to-date malware definitions to function effectively. The definitions database must exist and contain data.`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`
    agent_type `endpoint`
    tags `cis,windows,defender,antimalware,definitions`
META_END

DEF
    OBJECT defender_definitions
        path `C:\ProgramData\Microsoft\Windows Defender\Definition Updates\Backup\mpasbase.vdm`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE definitions_present
        exists boolean = true
        readable boolean = true
        size int > `0`
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN file_metadata
            TEST at_least_one all
            STATE_REF definitions_present
            OBJECT_REF defender_definitions
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
